    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-stakes slate today, with our priority placed firmly on stealing bases against favorable pitching deliveries. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.37) stands as our premier play; he benefits from an elite combination of a top-of-the-order spot and a generous 14% platoon edge against Cavalli. Similarly, **Caleb Durbin** (66.18) is a must-start, as his ability to capitalize on Scherzer\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his stolen base potential, making him a critical weapon in our scarcest category. **Christian Yelich** (65.44) also profiles as an elite option today, as his resurgence against right-handed pitching outweighs the moderate threat posed by Sasaki. While **Chase Meidroth** (62.45) lacks the household name recognition of others, his high efficiency against Abbott\u2019s 5.02 xERA makes him our most productive middle infielder for this matchup.\n\nWe are forced to navigate several lineup uncertainties, as **Gary Sanchez**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** all await official verification. Of the three, **Trea Turner** (60.86) remains locked in despite a \"Wind In\" penalty, as his speed metrics are essential for our Roto standing against Bradley. Conversely, **Kyle Schwarber** (57.64) sits near our \"marginal\" threshold; while his leadoff potential provides upside, he is the most susceptible to a cold day if the wind conditions worsen. Our bench is currently depleted by off-days for heavy hitters like **Yordan Alvarez** and **Junior Caminero**, meaning we have little room to pivot if these late-afternoon lineups shift. We are effectively betting on our high-speed, high-OBP archetypes like **Dillon Dingler** (55.92) to maintain our category floor while we wait for the rest of our roster, including **Lars Nootbaar**, **Nelson Velazquez**, and **Casey Schmitt**, to cycle back into active duty tomorrow.",
